# Build output
/dist/
/out/
/oekaki
/oekaki.exe

# Terraform working files. The example's plan.json is checked in on purpose:
# the repository has to run immediately after a clone.
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
tfplan
.terraform.lock.hcl

# Local configuration. A conventions file says where to look in somebody's
# repository — which local holds an account id, which file carries the account
# table. The values are only names, but the names describe the repository being
# read, and that repository is usually not this one's business.
#
# Ignored before anything invites people to write one: an ignore rule added
# afterwards does not help whoever already committed theirs.
*.conventions.yaml
*.conventions.yml
.oekaki.yaml
.oekaki.yml

# Editors and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Local agent state: machine-specific settings and scratch worktrees. Nothing
# here belongs to the project, and settings.local.json in particular records
# one person's local configuration.
.claude/
